Z||000007||p4n1c||07-06-2001||09:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>And if you knew anything about Tpac there was nothing wanna-be about him.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And if you knew anything about punk, you would know it will never die.  Because punk is not about the music, it's about the attitude and way of thinking.  Art can be punk, writing articles can be punk, etc, etc.<P>So don't go spouting off on something you know nothing about.  All it seems you know about the punk bands of today are the mainstream "diaper punk" bands.  <P>Don't even call Blink182 punk and that stupid movie Josie and the Pussycats is the industry trying to sell punk(which the band doesn't even do.  They were a pop band in the Archie comics).  NOFX, as I see 85blackGT listens too, is definitely not part of that, they have been around for a very long time(something like 1984), same with The Offspring(Officially formed 1986, and before you say they sold out, I have every single one of their albums and they sound the same since Ignition(Self-titled was definitly faster and harder)).  Try listening to punk other then the mainstream bands.  Listen to something like No Use for a Name, Larger than Life, etc.  And about the chick problems, that is <B>EMO</B> as in Emotional genre, not punk.  Get it right.<P>And to you 85blackGT, I hope that wasn't a racist comment, because if it was, you are definitely not punk.<P>I sick of the petty crap going on in this forum.  I know the census would be just to leave or ignore the posts, but this is getting stupid.  Steve just asked about a song, and people go about finding something to argue about.  So why don't you both take it to email or shut the f*** up.<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
